            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0609" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/23494.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Mediators.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 29, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: Answering the note
                    submitted by you and your colleagues, Ministers Naón and Suárez, I beg to say
                    that notice of General Huerta’s acceptance of mediation is received with
                    satisfaction. We note what you say in regard to suspension of hostilities during
                    mediation. We so understand it, provided of course that this Governnient would
                    be at liberty to repel any aggression attempted.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
